WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.260
PRIYANKA VERGADIA:
Welcome to "Get

00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:03.343
Cooking in Cloud," where
we share the best recipes

00:00:03.343 --> 00:00:04.830
to apply in your cloud kitchen.

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:06.995
I am Priyanka, and we
have a very special guest.

00:00:06.995 --> 00:00:08.370
CARTER MORGAN:
I'm Carter Morgan.

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:10.892
In this episode, we'll
be making a souffle.

00:00:10.892 --> 00:00:11.392
[CHUCKLING]

00:00:11.392 --> 00:00:13.434
PRIYANKA VERGADIA: Well,
that is a great metaphor

00:00:13.434 --> 00:00:16.020
because souffles have a
reputation of being complex

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:18.360
but are actually very
simple to prepare, just

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:20.780
like the theme of today's
show, migrating monoliths

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:22.835
to microservices-based
cloud applications.

00:00:22.835 --> 00:00:24.960
CARTER MORGAN: We're not
actually making a souffle?

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:25.790
PRIYANKA VERGADIA: Uh-uh.

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:26.290
No.

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:27.611
CARTER MORGAN: Oh.

00:00:27.611 --> 00:00:30.593
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.370
Imagine you're an
IT professional

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:42.520
in charge of a complex
website you need to modernize.

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:45.280
Imagine it's designed as
a monolith and it's time

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:46.660
to move to the cloud.

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:49.360
Maybe the way things have been
done is mostly working for you,

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:51.340
but when it comes time
to upgrade a service

00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:54.310
or add a new feature, you
start running into problems,

00:00:54.310 --> 00:00:56.170
like feature rollouts
taking forever

00:00:56.170 --> 00:00:57.700
because your
monolithic app can only

00:00:57.700 --> 00:00:59.250
be deployed once a quarter.

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:01.000
PRIYANKA VERGADIA:
Well, without a recipe,

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:03.580
it can be hard to know
exactly how to transition

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:07.030
your application in a way
that minimizes risk, downtime,

00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:09.970
and customer dissatisfaction
and also money lost.

00:01:09.970 --> 00:01:12.830
While modernizing your
platform by moving to the cloud

00:01:12.830 --> 00:01:14.710
and by switching
to microservices

00:01:14.710 --> 00:01:17.890
involves learning new tools
and new ways of working,

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:19.570
all of that can
seem overwhelming.

00:01:19.570 --> 00:01:21.640
CARTER MORGAN: But those
fears shouldn't stop you

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:24.280
from reaping the benefits of
a microservice-based cloud

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:25.120
platform.

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:26.620
You want to modernize
your platform

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:28.900
to provide a more nimble
and scalable environment

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:30.715
for the individual
features of the site,

00:01:30.715 --> 00:01:32.590
where the features can
be more easily managed

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:35.500
and updated than if they're
part of the monolithic platform.

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:38.000
Running in such an environment
leads to faster improvements.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:39.500
PRIYANKA VERGADIA:
Well, if you want

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:41.830
to just migrate everything
at once, that would

00:01:41.830 --> 00:01:43.480
be a lot of risk involved.

00:01:43.480 --> 00:01:46.420
But if you were to just
migrate feature by feature,

00:01:46.420 --> 00:01:48.473
you can avoid that
large amount of risk.

00:01:48.473 --> 00:01:50.890
CARTER MORGAN: There are three
main patterns for this type

00:01:50.890 --> 00:01:52.630
of migration to the cloud--

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:58.390
lift and shift, improve and
move, and rip and replace.

00:01:58.390 --> 00:02:00.360
We're going to use a
specific flavor of the rip

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:02.490
and replace pattern, where
the pattern is applied

00:02:02.490 --> 00:02:04.980
incrementally to each
feature of the application

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:06.900
rather than to the
application as a whole.

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:09.090
PRIYANKA VERGADIA:
Ooh, microservings.

00:02:09.090 --> 00:02:11.730
Over the next few videos, we
will use e-commerce website

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:13.200
as an example because--

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:15.015
CARTER MORGAN:
Veggies aren't fun.

00:02:15.015 --> 00:02:17.730
PRIYANKA VERGADIA: No,
Carter, because many of these

00:02:17.730 --> 00:02:20.040
are built with monolithic
proprietary tools

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:23.190
so they are really good
candidates for this migration.

00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:25.350
But even if you don't
have an e-commerce site,

00:02:25.350 --> 00:02:27.530
you can apply the principles
that we will cover here

00:02:27.530 --> 00:02:29.040
to a wide range of workloads.

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:31.320
CARTER MORGAN: In addition
to this migration pattern,

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:33.387
we'll show you two
hybrid patterns.

00:02:33.387 --> 00:02:35.220
During the migration
itself, the application

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:38.040
has a hybrid architecture
where some of the features

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:40.920
are in the cloud and some
are still on premises.

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:43.680
After the migration is finished,
the complete cloud application

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:45.420
is hosted in the
cloud, but it still

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:48.270
interacts with backend services
that remain on premises.

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:51.600
PRIYANKA VERGADIA: Wow, moving
to cloud could be messy.

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:52.930
Well, there you have it.

00:02:52.930 --> 00:02:55.440
If you're looking to migrate
your existing monolithic

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:57.360
platform to the
cloud, you've gotten

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:00.420
a taste of what's in store
for the rest of the series.

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:02.120
Stay tuned for
the next episode--

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:05.145
CARTER MORGAN: Where we will
actually make a souffle.

00:03:05.145 --> 00:03:06.138
PRIYANKA VERGADIA: No.

00:03:06.138 --> 00:03:08.430
CARTER MORGAN: Where we will
walk through the migration

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:08.855
process.

00:03:08.855 --> 00:03:09.870
PRIYANKA VERGADIA:
But if you are

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:12.180
excited to get on this
migration journey with us,

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:14.550
then don't forget to like
and subscribe to our channel.

00:03:14.550 --> 00:03:17.600
[MUSIC PLAYING]

